      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes a mechanism for ensuring safe file writes in the Grimoire system. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the prior state of that file (either its previous content, or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory journal. If an agent run fails for any reason\u2014such as exceeding a turn cap or encountering an unrecoverable error\u2014the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring files that previously existed or deleting newly created files. This gives each agent run atomic \u0022all-or-nothing\u0022 semantics for its writes without requiring a database transaction; the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of that single run.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent (which includes the agent that authored this response) doesn\u0027t actually use the rollback path, since it has no write capability at all\u2014though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5362,
      "output_tokens": 216
    }
